WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:44.730
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:44.730
Chapter 4

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.560
"There aren't many battles that had so
little meaning, yet brought so much fatigue."

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.500
Huh ?

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.540
This battle will be recorded
thusly by historians.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.980
What a disgrace.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.930
It's the disgrace of the Ministry
of the Military that led this battle.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.820
Lord Reinhard, you should think
only about your own feats.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.440
I see what you're saying, Kircheis,
but even that could be difficult...

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.070
...from what I can see from the way Luneberg
treated me in the admirals' conference.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.770
We destroyed 4 armored vehicles, killed
17 soldiers, and captured 7 soldiers.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:33.780
Other than that, though we did not catch him, we fatally wounded the enemy regimental commander.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.310
On the other hand, only 5 of
our soldiers were wounded.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:42.850
Also, we have discovered the location of their base from the data we gathered from those vehicles.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.520
I recommend a full-frontal ground
assault on the enemy base immediately.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.250
If we don't take the initiative,
the enemy will attack us.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:03:01.740
Since we can't coexist on this little satellite,
survival and victory are synonymous.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.320
I ask for the Commander's
courageous decision.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.900
What do you think,
Commodore Musel ?

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:20.030
Commander, you've appointed Commodore
Musel to be the sub-captain of my troops.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.850
The opinion of a sub-captain must
be the same as that of the captain's.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:29.080
It is unnecessary to ask for the sub-captain's
opinion at this table, if I may say so.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.530
Ah, of course.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.620
I think you're right.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.600
My mistake.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:45.680
It was as though he garnered the hostility and
antagonism of every admiral in that room.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.030
Because of him, I've become
less of a target of hatred...

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.000
...but I can't bring myself
to thank him for it.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.200
You've always been an object of people's
attention, in both good and bad ways.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:04.710
Because of Luneberg's emergence, I feel
as though I've become just a supporting actor.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.930
But he's a dangerous man.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:13.830
Using his accomplishments in
the present battle as leverage...

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:22.130
...he seized the upper-hand over the commander in order to take the initiative for the next battle plan.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:25.230
Furthermore, he's depriving you of
your right to speak at the conference...

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.270
...despite the fact that you
are of equal rank to him.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.460
This cutting-edge leadership may be his true character and he was just waiting for his chance.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.230
The three years since his defection during
which he has been slow in advancing...

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:41.500
...may have just been a
time of hibernation for him.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.660
In any case, he will
be an obstacle to us.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:55.210
Commodore Musel, in preparation
for our ground assault...

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.830
...I expect you to perform your
tasks to the best of your ability.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.370
I'm sure you will.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:04.060
I will make every effort not to
disappoint you, Commodore Luneberg.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.930
What a shrewd ass.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:15.540
He's planning to use me as an
ingredient for his own success.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:20.030
I'm growing weary of breathing
the same air as he does.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:22.700
Should we sabotage him, then ?

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.330
No, Kircheis.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:31.540
I don't mind being criticized for my self-confidence or being envied for my success...

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.050
...but I absolutely cannot stand
being labeled as incompetent.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:39.070
Much as I hate it, I'll perform my
tasks to the best of my ability.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.570
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.800
Damn.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:46.640
I never thought I had such a
knack for thankless duties.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.700
Kircheis, do you think I might
just be innately unlucky ?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:56.090
Even though I know that Luneberg
will take all the credit for my work...

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.340
...I'm still doing
the best job I can.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:06.000
Um, no, it's just that I thought this was
the first time I've heard you grumble.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.200
I've been appointed as the
interim regimental commander.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.740
The situation is perilous,
so I need your full obedience.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.390
If anyone has a
complaint, say it now.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.290
Salute the Acting Regimental Commander !

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:01.960
What do you think the size of the Imperial
army will be for their next attack ?

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:03.710
Don't know.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:07.710
But I bet it won't be smaller
than a team for flying ball.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.880
But let's be
serious about it.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.940
Estimating from the
size of their fleet...

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:19.550
...we can expect that they can move at least
a hundred thousand men for a ground assault.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.180
A hundred thousand ?

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:26.480
We have about
twenty thousand, at best.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:33.450
Plus, our troops are basically rear-line
reserves; the command system isn't in sync.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:39.010
Fortunately, the Rosenritter have high
morale and they'll follow your orders.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.960
But we probably can't expect much
cooperation from the other units.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:45.080
We can't worry
about the other units.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.800
They should look out for themselves.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:55.850
Der Decken, bring up the detailed
map of the area on the 3-D screen.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:08:01.780
And calculate the most
effective artillery angle.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:08.550
Blumhart, estimate the amount of necessary ammunition per cannon and prepare supplies.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.430
Linz, plan the positioning
of our armored units.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.810
Anyway, Colonel Luneberg
used to be such a dignified man.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.880
I wonder what complaints he had,
to defect back to the Empire.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.560
No idea.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.560
But there's one
thing I can say.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.320
I, too, am fed up with the current
predicament of the Alliance army.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.210
Of course, I've also felt angry
on more than one occasion...

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:42.530
...but isn't the situation in
the Empire worse than this ?

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.090
Luneberg probably
didn't think so.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.790
Right, I guess.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:52.260
And I think he was from
an aristocratic family.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:56.170
But you're from an
aristocratic family, too.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.230
Well, mine is a poor one,
just aristocratic in name.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:05.090
But the Lunebergs were on the
high end, with a court title, I think.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:08.480
He might have suddenly developed
nostalgia for class consciousness...

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.170
...and wanted to contribute
to his family line.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.340
Is that what happened ?

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:17.230
Well, forget about him for now.
We have a battle to prepare for.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:24.710
So, how long can we
sustain our defenses ?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.730
Are we only trying to
sustain our defenses ?

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:30.540
Outmoded weapons and
insufficient supplies...

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:34.680
...few soldiers and inaccurate
information, plus excessive anxiety.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.230
Though I'm a battle maniac...

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:41.980
...I'm not so optimistic as to think I can win in these conditions against an army five times larger than us.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.700
I've told headquarters to request
help from the fleet above us.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.610
If we can sustain our defenses until
the fleet arrives, that's good enough.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.680
But will Fleet HQ make a move ?

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.580
I don't know what the
Imperial Fleet is thinking...

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:02.220
...but practically, it's a big mistake
to station ships on the ground.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:07.580
I would think there are at least a few in the General Staff Office who are smart enough to realize that.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:12.700
I'm hoping they'll make a move; I don't care
if they're motivated by pure love of fame.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:18.170
If the General Staff Office
doesn't bother making a move ?

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:24.040
I'll make sure to reserve a portion of
land I like, to have my body buried there.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.400
I don't know
if I like that.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.330
Me neither.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:32.170
Instead of embracing the earth, I'd
rather think about embracing a woman.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.210
Commodore Musel.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:49.520
I've heard of your excellent
work in your assigned tasks.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:54.810
When we're young, we tend to be hasty and
look only at accomplishments on the battlefield.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.460
But preparation is
important in any battle.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.960
You know that very well.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.740
That's very commendable.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.360
Thank you, sir.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.740
Yes, yes.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.630
Very good.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:13.750
This is pitiful, Kircheis.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:17.130
Why do you say that,
out of the blue ?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.900
Think about it.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:24.870
Space is so enormous and history is so
grandiose, but I'm on this petty little planet...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.850
...and I'm doing this
petty little work.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:31.070
You don't like
Admiral Grimmelshausen ?

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:34.780
It's not an issue of
whether I like or dislike him.

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:37.200
But I'm not good with him.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.670
Especially because there's
a huge age gap between us.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:44.920
It's rare for Lord Reinhard to admit
difficulties dealing with someone.

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.830
Commodore Musel...

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:55.890
...we'll launch a full-frontal assault on
the rebel base at midnight on April 7th.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:12:00.900
Of course I'll lead the attack myself, but
you'll be accompanying us as a sub-captain.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:04.940
You've proven your capability
in battle preparation.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.950
I'd like to have you demonstrate the
same caliber of skill on the battlefield.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.190
I will.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.850
It can't be helped that Lord Reinhard's accomplishments will be recorded as Luneberg's.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:23.930
But if Luneberg shifts the blame for his mistakes onto Lord Reinhard that will truly be disastrous.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:28.680
I must watch out for Luneberg,
more than I do the enemy.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:57.250
Walter, have you ever thought about
getting married and having a family ?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.830
Family hates me.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:03.570
Don't worry.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:06.550
I'm not asking
you to marry me.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.010
I've done it once
and that was enough.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:14.030
It's just that I thought there must have been
many women who wanted to marry you.

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:15.580
That's all.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:21.280
"You'll be even more
disappointed if you marry me."

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.580
"So it's better to break
up before that happens."

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.130
That's what you're
thinking, isn't it ?

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:33.160
I said it on your behalf.
You should thank me.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.850
It ticks me off that I can't
quite say "you're dead wrong."

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:46.580
I've heard a bizarre rumor about your past
regimental commander, Colonel Luneberg.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:55.480
He married a lady of the Imperial aristocracy,
but he himself killed the fiancé of that woman.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.610
After he saw the picture of the
woman that the fiancé had...

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:02.980
...he fell in love, wanted to
have her and defected back.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.630
Do you believe that ?

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:09.940
That sounds like the delusion of a
love-sick girl who has never loved anyone.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:13.230
In reality, things aren't
all that schmaltzy...

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:18.870
...and if Luneberg were such a psychological diabetic he would have died a long time ago.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.230
See you later.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.060
Yeah.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.580
Bye.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.790
Seems like you were enjoying
yourself, Lt. Colonel Schenkopp.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:03.230
Winning a battle with a woman before
going into battle against the enemy, eh ?

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.190
Please don't confuse
the order of things.

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:12.420
It's not because I'm sleeping with a
woman that the enemy will attack us.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:18.050
If that were the case, the Empire
must think very highly of me.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.640
Good morning, Lt. Colonel.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.920
Hey, are we prepared ?

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.180
Perfectly.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:30.990
Are you okay ?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.700
The Base Commander
was so red with anger.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:38.490
He might have been offended, thinking
that I was making fun of his incompetence.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:42.130
But I never meant
he was incompetent.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:46.290
What I think is that he's not suited
for leading in actual combat.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:48.890
But I could care less
if he misunderstands me.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:55.070
I'm not the Vice Admiral,
but you are a dynamo, as always.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:02.800
But from what I heard, Blumhart, you haven't
known a woman yet, in a biblical sense.

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.740
Yes, that's true.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:11.070
It's a crime that a young man
has unused space in his bed.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:16.500
If you like, I can introduce you to a nice
woman, in preparation for the battle.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.700
Thank you.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:23.870
But, Lt. Colonel, my salary is still low
and it's too early for me to get married.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:27.850
I'm only 22 years old, and I haven't
found a woman I really like.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.290
Marriage ?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.830
My view of women is a little
bit different from yours.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:38.780
No, I don't mean to criticize
your views or anything.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:43.940
It's just something
I feel I want to do.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.500
It's weird,
perhaps, isn't it ?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.130
No, that's good.

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:51.580
Live on, Blumhart.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.750
And meet a nice woman.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:58.690
There's probably no better
reason to live than that.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:10.020
This is like eating
a half-baked fricassee.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.210
It makes me sick
to my stomach.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.300
Real battles will
take place from now on.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:21.830
I don't care for pure
decimation and destruction.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:28.790
I look for the likes of perfection of logic
and sophistication of art in battles.

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:36.290
This battle plan relies too much on
chance, and I have no power to change it.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.170
It's so frustrating.

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:44.220
This time around, please concentrate only
on your own personal feats on the battlefield.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.600
I know.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:50.230
That's what I intend to do, but I think that this
ground combat will trigger a chain reaction...

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:54.200
...that will affect the entire
battle at Van-Fleet Starzone.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:59.090
In the Empire, I'm probably
the only one who knows it.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:04.830
But I don't have command of a fleet,
or even of the ground troops.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.580
That's outrageous.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:08.830
Commodore Musel...

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:13.480
...before we shut down communications, I'd
like to hear your opinion before opening fire.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:19.470
There's not much to worry about as
far as the ground battle is concerned.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.480
There's a large
gap in our numbers...

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:24.920
...and we've done enough preparation
to utilize that numerical difference.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:33.180
But what we do need to worry about is that the enemy fleet may attack our fleet from orbit.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:39.360
If I get promoted, I'd like
to invite you to work for me.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:43.590
Your talent and leadership are
mature beyond your 18 years of age.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:50.800
I expect your cooperation as I fulfill my responsibility as a soldier of the Imperial forces.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:55.040
It's time.

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.830
We'll shut down radio communications
until the commencement of our operation.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.870
Do you hear that, Kircheis ?

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.740
He wants me to
work for him.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.230
Everyone despises me
because I'm too young...

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:09.230
...and belittle me because I'm
not from a high-ranked family...

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:11.230
...but he invites me
to be his subordinate.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:14.110
Is he acknowledging my talent ?

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:15.630
Did I gain a friend ?

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.260
What do you
think, Kircheis ?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.620
Lord Reinhard.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.960
Luneberg is no ordinary man.

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:31.340
But he's trying to make a dragon
become the minion of a snake.

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:34.390
That's worse than
an ordinary man.

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:40.320
But in any case, to whom is
this meeting more unfortunate ?

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:04.180
The Imperial ground
troops are closing in.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:08.110
Tanks, mobile rail cannons and
others - numbers cannot be estimated.

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:10.040
Open the communication line.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.480
We'll match the
radio frequency.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.540
To the Imperial army...

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:22.730
To the Imperial army, I order you
to quit launching useless attacks...

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:25.230
...raise both of your hands and
go back to where you belong.

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.780
If you do that, I won't
bother taking your lives.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.640
It's not too late now.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:35.110
In your homes, your lovers are
warming your beds and waiting for you !

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:41.550
It doesn't seem like the Imperial
troops will retreat, Lt. Colonel.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.550
I guess not.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.530
Even if I were the Imperial
commander, I wouldn't retreat either.

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:50.540
But at least I've done my
duty for their lovers at home.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:54.320
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp, what was
that communication about ?

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:59.470
If you open communications you're supposed to wait for the Imperial army's transmission first.

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:01.320
That was tremendously
stupid of you.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:06.870
I was only proposing a
gentlemanly and peaceful solution.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:11.440
What was so "gentlemanly"
and "peaceful" about that ?!

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:13.960
You're essentially selling
them an invitation for a fight !

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:17.290
They're the ones who came
all the way here to buy it.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:22.300
At least it's humane to sell them a
high-quality product at a high price.

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:24.640
That's funny.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:27.690
If they don't like the product,
they might return it.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:34.330
In any case, I strictly order you not
to cross into my area of responsibility.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.680
You're only supposed to do
what you're assigned to do.

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:40.810
There's no disagreement
here, is there ?

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:44.440
I understand,
Your Excellency, Base Commander.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:51.800
Well then, should we head back to our
assignment, to fulfill our responsibilities ?

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.340
I'll accompany you.

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:03.180
I guess the enemy troops have
got a jester of their own, Kircheis.

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:08.760
Look, Luneberg looks like he's
swallowed a few bitter bugs.

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:11.180
Lord Reinhard.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:25.220
This way, hurry.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:25.960
Hurry up.

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:07.420
I'd like to say,
"Stay somewhere safe."

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.970
But as advice you give on the
battlefield, it's as idiotic as it gets.

00:23:54.850 --> 00:23:55.940
How is it ?

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:58.540
They're positioning themselves strictly
in accordance with textbook strategies.

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:03.110
But of course that's only logical if you have numbers that are five times larger than your opposition.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:10.280
The tanks on the left flank
are a little too far ahead.

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:11.540
Make them retreat.

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:12.630
Incoming !

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:28.080
April 6th of Space Year 794,
Imperial Year 485...

00:24:28.080 --> 00:24:31.440
...this date was to be shaded
by the color of blood.

00:24:34.530 --> 00:24:41.150
The "real" Battle of Van-Fleet
Starzone may have begun on that date.

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:46.280
Bloodshed in April

